rustc: the EmiBSD targets, of the system and of the kernel

Why a patch: rustc knows nothing of EmiBSD. DevTools' rustc emits for the
system's targets aarch64-emibsd-emibsd and x86_64-emibsd-emibsd (D-0004,
D-0008) and for the kernel's aarch64-emibsd-none-softfloat and
x86_64-emibsd-none-softfloat (D-0008). For the system: the OS `emibsd` in
rustc_target's Os enum, a base `spec/base/emibsd.rs` stating what the ABI
asks of the target, which is the ABI its kernel and libc present (a
dynamic system of PIE executables, emulated TLS because its run-time
link-editor has no ELF TLS, full RELRO, frame pointers kept, structs
returned as integers, +crt-static honoured as a static PIE, the link
closed by the driver as for C, with compiler-rt's builtins around -lc,
which the libc's static archive relies on), the vendor
`emibsd`, and the two targets, whose LLVM triples carry the release the
ABI belongs to, aarch64-emibsd-emibsd8.0 and x86_64-emibsd-emibsd8.0
(the names of the targets do not, as x86_64-unknown-freebsd does not);
the x86_64 one takes the architecture's options as the other BSDs'
x86_64 targets do. For the kernel: upstream's bare-metal targets
aarch64-unknown-none-softfloat and x86_64-unknown-none with the vendor
`emibsd` and nothing else changed, so they emit the same code (LLVM keys
nothing on the vendor); both named -softfloat, which upstream's x86_64
one is without saying it. rustdoc names the OS "EmiBSD" in the
documentation's cfg notes. Tier 3 by upstream's rules. Written by EmiBSD
(ISC); carried by DevTools over the pinned tag, offered upstream when
stable. Author: Emilio Navarrete Lineros, 2026-10-31; amd64 and the
kernel's targets, 2026-11-02.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/compiler/rustc_target/src/spec/base/emibsd.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+use crate::spec::{FramePointer, Os, RelroLevel, TargetOptions, TlsModel, cvs};
+
+/// EmiBSD: the ABI its kernel and libc present, which is OpenBSD's (D-0003 of DevTools:
+/// written from the ABI, not copied); a dynamic system whose executables are PIE, with no
+/// ELF TLS in its run-time link-editor (emulated TLS), full RELRO, frame pointers kept for
+/// the kernel's and ld.so's backtraces.
+pub(crate) fn opts() -> TargetOptions {
+    TargetOptions {
+        os: Os::EmiBsd,
+        vendor: "emibsd".into(),
+        dynamic_linking: true,
+        families: cvs!["unix"],
+        has_rpath: true,
+        abi_return_struct_as_int: true,
+        position_independent_executables: true,
+        // +crt-static gives a static PIE (rcrt0.o): rustc asks the driver for -static-pie.
+        crt_static_respected: true,
+        static_position_independent_executables: true,
+        frame_pointer: FramePointer::Always,
+        relro_level: RelroLevel::Full,
+        default_dwarf_version: 2,
+        tls_model: TlsModel::Emulated,
+        // The driver closes the link as for C: compiler-rt's builtins around -lc, which the
+        // libc's static archive relies on (its amd64 assembly reads __cpu_features2 from them).
+        no_default_libraries: false,
+        ..Default::default()
+    }
+}
